          "note": "CodeRabbit fix: schema.sql revoked anon/authenticated on evidence_records and relied on RLS bypass for the service-role sync client, but table-level GRANTs and RLS are separate Postgres controls â€” RLS bypass does not imply a table-level privilege. Added an explicit 'grant select, insert, update, delete on evidence_records to service_role' so the upsert sync keeps working even on a project without Supabase's default service_role privileges (self-hosted Postgres+PostgREST, or a project with altered default privileges) instead of silently degrading to the local-only mirror on a 42501.",
          "version": "v4"
        },
        {
          "date": "2026-08-10",
          "note": "CodeRabbit fixes: find_prior_attempts now unions remote results with the local mirror instead of replacing it (a successful-but-empty remote query â€” schema.sql applied but not yet synced, or a lagging remote table â€” no longer silently hides a local match); write_local_index writes atomically (temp file + os.replace); _map_climb_ledger populates version_stamp from the source payload instead of hardcoding {}; schema.sql enables row-level security and revokes anon/authenticated access (the sync client's service-role key bypasses RLS, so this only closes the anonymous-read exposure of a table created in public).",
          "version": "v3"
        },
        {
          "date": "2026-08-10",
          "note": "Added compute_arm_fingerprint (records.py) as the single source of the climb-ledger-arm fingerprint domain; sync_evidence_store.py now calls it instead of inlining the hash (byte-identical output, verified by resync).",
          "version": "v2"
        },
