    "experiments.hf_screening": {
      "history": [
        {
          "date": "2026-08-10",
          "note": "CodeRabbit fixes: (1) ScreenConfig.max_minutes had no upper bound (only ge=1, default 30) while the repo's own MAX_RUN_MINUTES hard-run-cap law caps every run at 3 minutes and hf_jobs_train.py already enforces this exactly â€” hf_jobs_screen.py now caps max_minutes at MAX_RUN_MINUTES too, same as its sibling script. (2) collect_results' seed-file identity check omitted run_id and steps, so a stale seed_<n>.json from an earlier run at a different step count could pass identity and silently enter the aggregate; both are now part of the required identity match. (3) a seed file containing valid-but-non-object JSON (an array/scalar/null) crashed with AttributeError on payload.get(...) instead of degrading to incomplete like other malformed inputs â€” now guarded before the identity check.",
          "version": "v3"
        },
        {
          "date": "2026-08-10",
          "note": "CodeRabbit fixes (real security issues): ScreenConfig validates screen_id/metric/suite against a safe charset (they were interpolated into generated shell/Python script text â€” a crafted --config could otherwise inject shell commands or escape the intended bucket path); collect_results validates each seed file's identity (schema/screen_id/seed/suite/metric) before aggregating and requires a finite numeric value, so a stale or unrelated seed_<k>.json can no longer silently enter this screen's evidence; hf_jobs_train.ensure_hf_token_env aliases HUGGING_FACE_HUB_TOKEN to HF_TOKEN in-process before submission (never via a literal secret value on argv) so a caller with only that variable set still authenticates the remote job instead of silently starting one with no token.",
          "version": "v2"
        },
        {
          "date": "2026-08-09",
